# The grappling hook: thrown at what is under the crosshair (its key, Q), it flies (80 m/s, out to
# 40 m), takes hold of what it meets first and pulls you in on a rope reeled in at 4 m/s, so you
# swing. It holds anything but moves only you: the rope and the pull act on the player alone. Using
# it again, or a jump, lets go; it holds 2 s at most. A use while a line is out throws no other.

motion Throw on use if not linked
	until grapple.hook.used or pressed.jump
	lasts 2
	emit grapple.fired
	cast ray range 40 speed 80
		emit grapple.hooked
		link reel 4 alone
		force 160 top 15 ramp 0.1 on self along to
		move air_control 0.6 gravity 0 airborne 1

# The arm's throw (its animation pack's state machine reads motion.grapple.hook.Throwing).
motion Throwing on use if not linked
	lasts 0.45
